Third-party data used by this repository
=======================================

No dataset or scoring table is redistributed here. Everything is downloaded
by scripts/fetch_data.sh at the user's own request, and the terms below apply
to that data rather than to this code. Read them before using this repository
for anything commercial.

CFD mismatch and PAM tables
---------------------------
Origin: Doench et al. 2016, Nature Biotechnology 34(2):184-191,
doi:10.1038/nbt.3437, Supplementary Table 19.

Obtained from third-party vendored copies, since there is no official
machine-readable release. The copy in maximilianh/crisporWebsite under
CFD_Scoring/ states that use is free only for academic or non-profit
organisations and that commercial use requires a separate license.

Consequence for this repository: data/cfd_mismatch.tsv and data/cfd_pam.tsv
are NOT committed. They are generated locally by scripts/import_cfd.py from a
copy the user downloads. To use this work commercially, obtain the weights
under terms that permit it, or substitute a differently licensed scoring
model. The code path for that already exists, since any TSV with the same
columns loads in their place.

CHANGE-seq measured off-target data
-----------------------------------
Origin: Lazzarotto et al. 2020, Nature Biotechnology 38:1317-1327,
doi:10.1038/s41587-020-0555-7. GEO accession GSE149295, BioProject
PRJNA625995.

Obtained in processed form from github.com/OrensteinLab/SysEvalOffTarget.

Bulge-aligned datasets and the refined TrueOT benchmark
-------------------------------------------------------
Origin: Yaish and Orenstein 2024, Nucleic Acids Research 52(12):6777-6790,
doi:10.1093/nar/gkae428. Code and data at
github.com/OrensteinLab/CRISPR-Bulge, archived at Zenodo
doi:10.5281/zenodo.10902355.

The refined TrueOT benchmark derives from TrueOT, curated by the Bao lab at
Rice University, github.com/baolab-rice/CRISPR_OT_scoring.

Check each source's own license before redistribution. This repository asserts
no rights over any of them.
